	array(
		'question_text'  => 'A registered AMFT maintains a website and social-media profile using a nickname and the abbreviation “AMFT.” The pages omit the registered AMFT’s Board-filed name, employer, registration number, complete registration title, and statement that the registered AMFT is supervised by a licensed person. What is the best corrective action?',
		'option_a'       => 'Correct every professional platform to include all required information, while using the nickname only alongside the Board-filed name.',
		'option_b'       => 'Add the registration number to the website and leave the social-media profile unchanged because space is limited.',
		'option_c'       => 'Replace the professional pages with a disclaimer stating that online information should not be treated as advertising.',
		'option_d'       => 'List the supervisor’s name alone because supervision information substitutes for the registered AMFT’s own registration details.',
		'correct_option' => 'a',
		'explanation'    => 'A. Correct. California advertising rules apply broadly to websites and social media. A registered AMFT must ensure that required identifying, employment, registration, and supervision information is complete and easy to find; a nickname does not replace the Board-filed name.
B. Incorrect. Registration number alone is insufficient, and social media is also advertising. Required information cannot be omitted merely because the platform has limited space.
C. Incorrect. A disclaimer does not remove a professional communication from the advertising rules or cure missing required information.
D. Incorrect. Supervisor information does not substitute for the registered AMFT’s own name, title, registration number, employer, and supervision statement.
CTA EXAM STRATEGY: Treat each public professional profile as advertising and check every required identity and supervision element.',
	),
	array(
		'question_text'  => 'A therapist places expired paper treatment records into an ordinary office trash container.What is the most significant concern?',
		'option_a'       => 'The records may have been retained for too long without further assessment of the governing facts.',
