		'option_d'       => 'Assume the client is not trying hard enough without further assessment of the governing facts while treating that single factor as controlling.',
		'correct_option' => 'b',
		'explanation'    => 'A. Incorrect. General evidence informs care but does not justify ignoring sustained client-specific deterioration.
B. Correct. This uses outcome information to conduct a comprehensive but proportionate review and preserve continuity.
C. Incorrect. Abrupt termination may create additional harm when a reasoned modification or orderly transition is available.
