	array(
		'question_text'  => 'A registered AMFT is treating a client with a rapidly worsening eating disorder. The registered AMFT has limited specialized training, feels unusually protective of the client, and has relied on an informal peer consultant instead of promptly involving the approved supervisor. The client now reports fainting and severe restriction. What is the best response?',
