		'correct_option' => 'b',
		'explanation'    => 'A. Incorrect. Licensure, general experience, and confidence do not overcome the absence of directly relevant preparation or the possible effect of personal reactions.
B. Correct. This integrates the chapter’s core sequence: identify the actual gaps, evaluate the clinician factors, assess client risk, and select a safe proportionate response.
